  "notes": "A formal, legal-register word. The object being violated is marked with を, and the pattern is 〜を{侵害|しんがい}する. Commonly paired with words for rights ({権利|けんり}), territory ({領土|りょうど}), and privacy.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{人権|じんけん}{侵害|しんがい} (human rights violation)\n・{著作権|ちょさくけん}{侵害|しんがい} (copyright infringement)\n・{権利|けんり}{侵害|しんがい} (infringement of rights)\n・{領土|りょうど}{侵害|しんがい} (territorial encroachment)\n・{侵害|しんがい}{行為|こうい} (act of infringement)",
